  "body": " Algebra detected by exponents   Let be a semigroup and .   is an integral domain, and its fraction field is the fraction field of .  is a finitely generated -algebra if and only if is finitely generated.  If these finite generation conditions hold, .     The embedding in the Laurent polynomial ring proves that is a domain. Every is with , so belongs to its fraction field. This proves the first assertion.  Semigroup generators give algebra generators. Conversely, suppose that finitely many polynomials generate as an algebra. Let be the finite union of their supports. All polynomials in these generators have support in . Since each , , must be such a polynomial, linear independence of Laurent monomials implies . Thus . The final assertion follows from the first, because the fraction field of is a rational function field of transcendence degree .   "
