  "body": " A nonzero character in the kernel  The fan with rays and in gives . Its maximal cones have dimension one, while the variety has dimension two. For its two boundary divisors, The subgroup is the kernel, corresponding to the global units in the second coordinate, modulo constants.  The cokernel is , with . The cones are smooth, so , and . An initial zero in the character-to-divisor sequence would therefore give an incorrect statement even in this smooth example.  "
