  "title": "Hirzebruch surfaces before intersection theory.",
  "body": " Hirzebruch surfaces before intersection theory  For , use the cyclic rays with maximal cones spanned by adjacent pairs. This is the Hirzebruch fan. Every adjacent determinant is , so all Weil divisors on are Cartier. The character relations are They give . Set and ; then .  The projection , , is compatible with the fan of and defines the ruling. The divisors are its two invariant fibers, and the quotient fans show that map isomorphically to the base. This explains the notation without presupposing intersection numbers.  For , the support data on cones are They agree on common rays and give value on . The parameter is already visible in the transition characters, although the abstract Picard group is always . Summing the boundary classes yields Positivity and intersection numbers will require the additional constructions of the next chapters; none has been used here.  "
