  "number": "4.15",
  "title": "Polytopes and ample polarizations.",
  "body": " Polytopes and ample polarizations   Let . For each ray of the normal fan put Then is Cartier and ample, and . Conversely, an invariant ample Cartier divisor on a complete toric variety has a full-dimensional lattice polytope whose normal fan is precisely the original fan.    On the normal cone of a vertex , the support function is the integral linear form . These give Cartier data. The minimum is attained at exactly on that normal cone, giving strict concavity and therefore ampleness. The facet inequalities recover .  Conversely generation makes the convex hull of the Cartier points. Strict concavity says that the vectors where minimizes pairing are exactly , identifying the normal fan. The polytope has full dimension: the proof of ampleness puts and in a sufficiently large dilate, and those differences generate as a group. Its affine span is therefore .   "
