  "type": "Proposition",
  "number": "4.17",
  "title": "Projective normality is integer decomposition.",
  "body": " Projective normality is integer decomposition   If is very ample, the embedding by its complete linear system is projectively normal if and only if is normal. For an ample divisor, sufficiently large multiples are both very ample and normally generated.    The homogeneous coordinate ring of the embedding is the degree-one generated subring of . Its degree- exponents are sums of lattice points of . Its group of exponent differences is : on the affine chart at a vertex, very ampleness makes the differences of section weights generate , hence the whole character lattice as a group, and one degree-one point supplies the degree direction. The semigroup normalization theorem now identifies its integral closure with . Equality is exactly the integer decomposition property.  The dilation theorem for lattice polytopes states that if , then is normal for every ; see . Segments and points are already normal. Combine this with sufficiently large very ample multiples from the ample criterion.   "
