  "type": "Theorem",
  "number": "4.22",
  "title": "Finite generation produces a toric degeneration.",
  "body": " Finite generation produces a toric degeneration   Let be a projective variety over , and let a very ample linear system give a closed immersion. For its homogeneous coordinate ring take the valuation from an admissible complete flag. If the semigroup is finitely generated, there is a flat family over whose nonzero fibers are isomorphic to and whose zero fiber is . The special fiber can be nonnormal. Its normalization is the normal toric variety determined by the value polytope with its intrinsic lattice. Here that polytope is the degree-one slice of the closed value cone; it uses values of the stated homogeneous coordinate ring.   "
