  "title": "A wall relation gives a curve functional.",
  "body": " A wall relation gives a curve functional  For , the vector is a positive rational multiple of this relation, with zero entries on other rays. Consequently If both adjacent cones are smooth, normalize ; then . For singular cones, lattice indices determine the factor and it must not be omitted.  Divisors outside the two adjacent cones are disjoint from . Intersecting principal character divisors with gives a relation among the remaining ray vectors. This relation space is one dimensional. Each extra divisor meets at its corresponding endpoint without containing the curve. A positive Cartier multiple therefore restricts to a nonzero effective divisor, giving positive intersection and fixing the sign of proportionality. In smooth coordinates each endpoint intersection is transverse with multiplicity one, proving that normalization.  "
