  "number": "11.2",
  "title": "The weighted initial family is flat.",
  "body": " The weighted initial family is flat  The algebra is finitely generated and flat over , with Under the second isomorphism the coordinate maps to . In particular, every fiber at is isomorphic to .  Consider the homomorphism Every maps to zero. To prove that these generate the kernel, group a polynomial by the integer of a term . Its group of index is The Laurent powers of are independent over , so . For a nonzero group, the smallest actual -exponent in it is . Hence Summing the groups proves .  Thus is the image algebra, generated by and the finitely many . As a -module it embeds in . The latter is torsion-free: choose a -basis of and regard it as a direct sum of copies of . Consequently is torsion-free over the PID , and is flat. Indeed a torsion-free module over a PID is the directed union of its finitely generated submodules, each of which is free; a directed colimit of flat modules is flat. No finite generation as a module is required.  Reducing the generators of modulo gives precisely . After inverting , all belong to the image by multiplication with , proving the second isomorphism and the assertions about fibers.  "
