  "title": "Lower lifts and their simplicial complex.",
  "body": " Lower lifts and their simplicial complex  Lift to and project the lower faces of their convex hull back to . A lower face is one minimizing a linear functional whose last-coordinate coefficient is positive. For generic weights these projected cells are simplices, defining a regular triangulation . Regard it as a simplicial complex on the labelled index set ; an index need not occur as a vertex of any cell. Its Stanley Reisner ideal is A full-dimensional simplex with index set is unimodular when its columns form a basis of . Equivalently, its normalized volume in the affine lattice of is one.  "
