  "body": " Lattice coordinates and products   If is a lattice isomorphism, then . If two varieties in our class have preferred polytopes , their product has preferred polytope , with    A lattice isomorphism has determinant of absolute value one in lattice coordinates. Change of variables therefore preserves normalized volume and transforms the vector integral by , proving the first identity. The rays of the product fan have the form or . Their anticanonical inequalities separate into the inequalities defining the two factors, giving exactly the product polytope. Fubini's theorem gives its volume and both components of its first moment, proving the remaining formulas.   "
